# Compiler output. Every file ignored here is produced by a named npm script —
# `evgpdf:compile`, `evghtml:compile`, `evgjson:compile`, `pdf-tool:cli:png` and
# the rest — so a clone rebuilds it rather than carrying it. They were tracked
# until now, and 170 000 lines of regenerated bundle in a diff is what that cost:
# a twelve-line source change arrived as a file nobody could review.
#
# Seven files in this directory are still tracked, deliberately. Nothing in
# package.json builds them, so ignoring them would be losing them, not tidying
# them: component_engine_module.cjs, evg_html_tool.go, evg_raster_test.js,
# evg_raster_text_test.js, evg_single_char_test.js, progressive_jpeg_test.js,
# variant.hpp. (evg_html_tool.go is the odd one: evghtml:compile writes the
# JavaScript only, so whatever produced the Go is not in package.json.) Git keeps
# tracking a file it already tracks whatever this file says, so they are safe
# where they are — but if you work out which source produces one, give it a
# compile script and it can go too.
*.js
*.cjs
*.go
*.cpp
*.rs
*.hpp
